{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/915134-exchanging-souls-not-pacting-them","id":915134,"title":"Exchanging Souls, Not Pacting Them","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-15T15:26:29-07:00","id":915134,"title":"Exchanging Souls, Not Pacting Them","content":"Soul Pacts extinguish (absorb?) a Mortal's life. It turns them into a Cover for the Demon to use.<br /> <br /> Would it fit in Demon lore, and the mechanics to instead do a trade? Essentially, the Demon gets the Mortal's life, and in exchange, the Mortal becomes one of their Covers, just as permanently as a Soul Pact. Mr. Steele the high-flying corporate consultant is no longer the Cover of the Demonic Inquisitor Vandelium, but Joseph Steele, whole and flesh.<br /> <br /> Is this something that should be a Exploit or just fall into Pact rules as is? Or is it missing the theme of Demon by allowing trades?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T17:14:18-07:00","id":915201,"title":"","content":"Maybe that should be an Exploit, since it fits in the ideas of Demon but it steps a bit outside the baseline rules for Covers (much like how Ephemeral Cover makes for a normally impossible type of Cover).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"us